xt": "The 10k's F5 lost 10.4 points and pushed Black's lead to +14.0, the highest of the game. White's stone sits right beside Black's E5 and below G7, so the centre was suddenly open to attack."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "Opus 5.5 answered with G5, the worst move of the game: 13.2 points lost, from +14.0 down to +0.8. The engine wanted E8. A 14-point lead was gone in one move."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "F3 lost another 8.9 points and moved the lead from +5.1 to -3.8. The engine's choice was G4, the point Opus 5.5 only took at move 21 (3.3 lost). White's F4, F5 and F6 stones had become a wall down the F file. From here Black was always behind."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and compute group liberties and an area count of the current position, with no candidate-move loop or lookahead. The remaining commands were grep and a Python script that edited CLAUDE.md and games.md, which are notes and game logs.", "stop": false}}